==Spanish==

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr|+<audio:LL-Q1321 (spa)-AdrianAbdulBaha-loco.wav;Audio (Colombia)>}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|es|osp|loco}}, perhaps from {{der|es|xaa|لَوْقَاء|tr=láwqa}}, from {{der|es|ar|لَوْقَاء}}, feminine singular form of {{m|ar|أَلْوَق||stupid}},<ref>{{R:es:DCECH|loco|683|vol=G-Ma}}</ref> by reinterpreting the final Andalusian Arabic ''-a'' as the Ibero-Romance ''-a'' and back-forming the masculine with ''-o''. Edward Roberts thinks the term is related to {{der|es|ar|لَاق||to soften}},<ref>{{R:es:Roberts:2014}}</ref> but this verb is of root ''l-y-q'', not ''l-w-q'' like {{m|ar||أَلْوَق}}. Alternatively, derived from {{der|es|grc|γλαυκός|t=clear}}. Compare {{cog|pt|louco}} and {{cog|scn|loccu}}.

====Adjective====
{{es-adj|sup=loquísimo}}

# [[crazy]], [[insane]], [[mad]], [[nuts]] {{q|asserting that something is out of place in the head}}
#: {{syn|es|chiflado|desquiciado|pirado|trastornado}}
#: {{uxi|es|Estoy '''loco''' por ti.|I am '''crazy''' for you, madly in love with you.}}
#: {{uxi|es|David está muy '''loco'''.|David's really '''crazy'''.}}
#: {{uxi|es|Lorena se pone algo '''loca''' cuando bebe.|Lorena gets a bit '''crazy''' when she drinks [alcohol].}}
# [[rash]], [[risky]], [[imprudent]]
#: {{syn|es|alocado|arrebatado|atolondrado|imprudente|insensato}}
#: {{uxi|es|una decisión loca de último momento|a '''rash''' decision taken at the last minute}}
#: {{uxi|es|No sean '''locos''', tómense su tiempo.|Don't be '''imprudent''', take your time.}}
# [[tremendous]], [[terrific]], [[huge]], [[enormous]]
#: {{syn|es|enorme|grande|tremendo}}
#: {{uxi|es|Tuviste una suerte '''loca''' al ganar la rifa.|You had some '''huge''' luck when winning the raffle.}}
# [[malfunctioning]], [[broken]] and working [[incorrectly]] {{q|said of a machine}}
#: {{uxi|es|El reloj de la abuela se ha vuelto '''loco'''.|Grandma's clock has started malfunctioning.}}
# [[overgrown]], [[rambling]]
#: {{syn|es|descuidado}}
#: {{uxi|es|Los arbustos se ven '''locos''', deberías podarlos.|The bushes look '''overgrown''' now, you should trim them.}}
#: {{uxi|es|El cabello se te ve '''loco''', ve a cortártelo.|Your hair looks '''overgrown''', go get a haircut.}}
# [[loose]] {{q|pipe fittings, pulley}}
#: {{syn|es|flojo|suelto}}
# {{lb|es|colloquial}} [[sexy]] {{q|only with [[ser#Spanish|ser]]}}
#: {{uxi|es|Pero qué loca es, qué loca se ve.|She's so sexy, she looks so sexy.}}

